 <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:51:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: gs201: Add the MFC
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Describe the gs201 MFC (v15.6), disabled, from Google's MFC-0 node
(kernel/devices/google/gs201, dts/gs201-mfc.dtsi, branch
android-gs-pantah-6.1-android16): registers at 0x1c8d0000, GIC SPI 504
level high.

Its "mfc" clock is the ACPM firmware's MFC DVFS domain, so that s5p-mfc
can raise the rate while it decodes instead of running at the 100 MHz
the bootloader leaves; ACPM sets the voltage with it.

The two System MMUs in front of it are not described: they stay in
bypass, so the MFC sees physical addresses through 32-bit registers, and
a board that enables it gives it memory below 4 GiB through
memory-region. No power domain and no CMU_MFC gates either: CMU_MFC is
not described yet, and the gs201 boards boot with clk_ignore_unused and
pd_ignore_unused, which leave them on as the bootloader set them. The
node's comment names the CMU_TOP gate that depends on that flag.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ángel René <17342133+angelrenefm@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
index 4f804ecbb..11f0d479e 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/gs201.dtsi
@@ -2013,6 +2013,26 @@ dsi0_in: endpoint {
 			};
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * MFC v15.6 video codec. Its two System MMUs (0x1c870000,
+		 * 0x1c8a0000) are left in bypass and CMU_MFC is not described
+		 * yet, so the firmware and its buffers need memory below 4 GiB
+		 * from the board's memory-region, and the block runs on the
+		 * power domain the bootloader leaves on. Its rate (and voltage)
+		 * is the ACPM firmware's MFC DVFS domain. CMU_TOP's
+		 * gout_cmu_mfc_mfc gate feeds the block too and stays on only
+		 * because the boards boot with clk_ignore_unused: without that
+		 * flag the first register access would hit an unclocked block.
+		 */
+		mfc: video-codec@1c8d0000 {
+			compatible = "google,gs201-mfc";
+			reg = <0x1c8d0000 0x10000>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 504 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
+			clocks = <&acpm_ipc GS201_CLK_ACPM_DVFS_MFC>;
+			clock-names = "mfc";
+			status = "disabled";
+		};
+
 		gpu: gpu@28000000 {
 			compatible = "google,gs201-mali", "arm,mali-valhall-csf";
 			reg = <0x28000000 0x480000>;
